# Legal work product — evidence packs, demand-letter responses, and verbatim
# source captures of competitor websites. Kept on disk and archived outside
# the repo, deliberately NOT version-controlled:
#   - they are privileged/sensitive material that does not belong in a clone
#     handed to a contractor or pushed to a hosting provider
#   - the source captures are third parties' pages and carried live Google API
#     keys, which is what tripped GitHub secret scanning on 2026-08-02
/docs/legal

# Nothing log-shaped belongs in the web root. A laravel.log downloaded from
# the log viewer was found sitting in public/ carrying the proxy password and
# both captcha keys (2026-08-02) — served at 200 by the dev server.
/public/*.log
/public/*.sql
/public/*.env
